          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid winning tricks that contain point-bearing cards. The first player to reach 121 points loses the match.',
          gameplay: 'The pitcher leads to the first trick; the suit led becomes trump for the hand. Players must follow suit if able, otherwise may play any card. Highest card of led suit wins unless trump is played, then highest trump wins. Trick winner leads next trick. Points are pegged during play for certain trump cards and all fives; after all 13 tricks, card points are counted and the player with highest total pegs the Eight bonus.',
          keyRules: [
            'Trump is not preselected: it is set by the suit of the first card led by the pitcher.',
            'A 13-card dummy hand is out of play each deal and can contain scoring cards.',
            'If pegging from a trick takes a player to 121 or more, the game ends immediately and that player loses.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Dump dangerous cards, especially fives and high trumps, when you can lose tricks safely.',
          intermediate: 'As pitcher, lead a suit where you are weak to avoid controlling too many early tricks.',
          advanced: 'Track opponent peg totals and force near-121 players into compulsory wins containing scoring cards.',
          tips: [
            'The 5 of trumps (10 points) and 9 of trumps (9 points) are the biggest immediate hazards.',
            'Late in the hand, preserving low non-trumps can help you duck forced wins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
